The answer is **downstream = 4 hours, upstream = 5.6 hours**.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('mathx-q00236', 'math-aptitude-bank-2', 'Time, Speed, Distance & Work', 3, 37, 'A boat has a speed of 15 km/h in still water, and the speed of the stream is 3 km/h. Find the time taken by the boat to travel 72 km downstream and the time to travel the same distance upstream.', 'Downstream speed is `boat speed + stream speed = 15 + 3 = 18` km/h, and upstream speed is `boat speed - stream speed = 15 - 3 = 12` km/h.

