The answer is **x = 6, y = 4**.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('mathx-q00290', 'math-aptitude-bank-2', 'Algebra & Geometry', 4, 25, 'Solve the simultaneous equations: `5x + 2y = 33` and `2x + +3y = 22`.', 'Using elimination or substitution, solve the two linear equations for `x` and `y`.

Solving `5x + 2y = 33` and `2x + 3y = 22` simultaneously gives `x = 5` and `y = 4`.

The answer is **x = 5, y = 4**.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('mathx-q00291', 'math-aptitude-bank-2', 'Algebra & Geometry', 4, 26, 'If `3/4 = 15/x`, find the value of x.', 'Cross-multiplying the proportion gives `3 × x = 4 × 15`.

So `x = (4 × 15) / 3 = 60 / 3 = 20`.

The answer is **x = 20**.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('mathx-q00292', 'math-aptitude-bank-2', 'Algebra & Geometry', 4, 27, 'If `5/6 = 30/x`, find the value of x.', 'Cross-multiplying the proportion gives `5 × x = 6 × 30`.

So `x = (6 × 30) / 5 = 180 / 5 = 36`.

The answer is **x = 36**.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('mathx-q00293', 'math-aptitude-bank-2', 'Algebra & Geometry', 4, 28, 'If `2/7 = 14/x`, find the value of x.', 'Cross-multiplying the proportion gives `2 × x = 7 × 14`.

So `x = (7 × 14) / 2 = 98 / 2 = 49`.

The answer is **x = 49**.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('mathx-q00294', 'math-aptitude-bank-2', 'Algebra & Geometry', 4, 29, 'If `9/4 = 36/x`, find the value of x.', 'Cross-multiplying the proportion gives `9 × x = 4 × 36`.

So `x = (4 × 36) / 9 = 144 / 9 = 16`.

The answer is **x = 16**.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('mathx-q00295', 'math-aptitude-bank-2', 'Algebra & Geometry', 4, 30, 'If `7/8 = 56/x`, find the value of x.', 'Cross-multiplying the proportion gives `7 × x = 8 × 56`.

So `x = (8 × 56) / 7 = 448 / 7 = 64`.

The answer is **x = 64**.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('mathx-q00296', 'math-aptitude-bank-2', 'Algebra & Geometry', 4, 31, 'Using the remainder theorem, find the remainder when `1x^2 + (-3)x + (2)` is divided by `(x - 2)`.', 'By the remainder theorem, the remainder when a polynomial `p(x)` is divided by `(x - a)` equals `p(a)`.

`p(2) = 1 × 2^2 + (-3) × 2 + (2) = 0`.

The answer is **0**.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('mathx-q00297', 'math-aptitude-bank-2', 'Algebra & Geometry', 4, 32, 'Using the remainder theorem, find the remainder when `2x^2 + (5)x + (-1)` is divided by `(x - -1)`.', 'By the remainder theorem, the remainder when a polynomial `p(x)` is divided by `(x - a)` equals `p(a)`.

`p(-1) = 2 × -1^2 + (5) × -1 + (-1) = -4`.

The answer is **-4**.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('mathx-q00298', 'math-aptitude-bank-2', 'Algebra & Geometry', 4, 33, 'Using the remainder theorem, find the remainder when `1x^2 + (2)x + (-8)` is divided by `(x - 3)`.', 'By the remainder theorem, the remainder when a polynomial `p(x)` is divided by `(x - a)` equals `p(a)`.

`p(3) = 1 × 3^2 + (2) × 3 + (-8) = 7`.

The answer is **7**.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('mathx-q00299', 'math-aptitude-bank-2', 'Algebra & Geometry', 4, 34, 'Using the remainder theorem, find the remainder when `3x^2 + (-4)x + (1)` is divided by `(x - 1)`.', 'By the remainder theorem, the remainder when a polynomial `p(x)` is divided by `(x - a)` equals `p(a)`.

`p(1) = 3 × 1^2 + (-4) × 1 + (1) = 0`.

The answer is **0**.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('mathx-q00300', 'math-aptitude-bank-2', 'Algebra & Geometry', 4, 35, 'Using the remainder theorem, find the remainder when `1x^2 + (-6)x + (9)` is divided by `(x - 4)`.', 'By the remainder theorem, the remainder when a polynomial `p(x)` is divided by `(x - a)` equals `p(a)`.

`p(4) = 1 × 4^2 + (-6) × 4 + (9) = 1`.

The answer is **1**.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('mathx-q00301', 'math-aptitude-bank-2', 'Algebra & Geometry', 4, 36, 'A right triangle has legs of length 3 cm and 4 cm. Find the length of the hypotenuse.', 'By the Pythagorean theorem, `hypotenuse^2 = a^2 + b^2`.

`hypotenuse = √(3^2 + 4^2) = √(9 + 16) = √25 = 5` cm.

The answer is **5 cm**.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('mathx-q00302', 'math-aptitude-bank-2', 'Algebra & Geometry', 4, 37, 'A right triangle has legs of length 6 cm and 8 cm. Find the length of the hypotenuse.', 'By the Pythagorean theorem, `hypotenuse^2 = a^2 + b^2`.

`hypotenuse = √(6^2 + 8^2) = √(36 + 64) = √100 = 10` cm.

The answer is **10 cm**.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('mathx-q00303', 'math-aptitude-bank-2', 'Algebra & Geometry', 4, 38, 'A right triangle has legs of length 5 cm and 12 cm. Find the length of the hypotenuse.', 'By the Pythagorean theorem, `hypotenuse^2 = a^2 + b^2`.

`hypotenuse = √(5^2 + 12^2) = √(25 + 144) = √169 = 13` cm.

The answer is **13 cm**.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('mathx-q00304', 'math-aptitude-bank-2', 'Algebra & Geometry', 4, 39, 'A right triangle has legs of length 9 cm and 12 cm. Find the length of the hypotenuse.', 'By the Pythagorean theorem, `hypotenuse^2 = a^2 + b^2`.

`hypotenuse = √(9^2 + 12^2) = √(81 + 144) = √225 = 15` cm.

The answer is **15 cm**.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('mathx-q00305', 'math-aptitude-bank-2', 'Algebra & Geometry', 4, 40, 'A right triangle has legs of length 8 cm and 15 cm. Find the length of the hypotenuse.', 'By the Pythagorean theorem, `hypotenuse^2 = a^2 + b^2`.

`hypotenuse = √(8^2 + 15^2) = √(64 + 225) = √289 = 17` cm.

The answer is **17 cm**.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('mathx-q00306', 'math-aptitude-bank-2', 'Algebra & Geometry', 4, 41, 'In a triangle, two of the angles measure 50° and 60°. Find the third angle.', 'The sum of the interior angles of a triangle is always `180°`.

