The answer is **0**.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('mathx-q00431', 'math-aptitude-bank-2', 'Trigonometry & Data Interpretation', 6, 34, 'Evaluate: `2 sin 30° cos 30°`.', 'Use the standard trigonometric values for 30°, 45°, 60°, and 90°.

This is `sin(2×30°) = sin 60° = √3/2` by the double angle formula.

The answer is **0.87**.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('mathx-q00432', 'math-aptitude-bank-2', 'Trigonometry & Data Interpretation', 6, 35, 'Evaluate: `tan 45° + tan 60°`.', 'Use the standard trigonometric values for 30°, 45°, 60°, and 90°.

Substituting `tan 45° = 1` and `tan 60° = √3` directly gives `1 + √3`.

The answer is **2.73**.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('mathx-q00433', 'math-aptitude-bank-2', 'Trigonometry & Data Interpretation', 6, 36, 'Evaluate: `sin² 60° + cos² 60°`.', 'Use the standard trigonometric values for 30°, 45°, 60°, and 90°.

This is the Pythagorean identity `sin²θ + cos²θ = 1`, true for any angle.

The answer is **1**.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('mathx-q00434', 'math-aptitude-bank-2', 'Trigonometry & Data Interpretation', 6, 37, 'Evaluate: `cos 60° × cos 30° − sin 60° × sin 30°`.', 'Use the standard trigonometric values for 30°, 45°, 60°, and 90°.

This is `cos(60°+30°) = cos 90° = 0` by the cosine addition formula.

The answer is **0**.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('mathx-q00435', 'math-aptitude-bank-2', 'Trigonometry & Data Interpretation', 6, 38, 'Evaluate: `tan 60° ÷ tan 30°`.', 'Use the standard trigonometric values for 30°, 45°, 60°, and 90°.

Substituting `tan 60° = √3` and `tan 30° = 1/√3` gives `√3 ÷ (1/√3) = 3`.

The answer is **3**.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('mathx-q00436', 'math-aptitude-bank-2', 'Trigonometry & Data Interpretation', 6, 39, 'Evaluate: `sin 90° − 2 sin² 45°`.', 'Use the standard trigonometric values for 30°, 45°, 60°, and 90°.

Substituting `sin 90° = 1` and `sin 45° = 1/√2` gives `1 - 2×(1/2) = 0`.

The answer is **0**.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
INSERT INTO questions (id, set_id, topic_label, topic_order, sort_order, q, a, created_at) VALUES ('mathx-q00437', 'math-aptitude-bank-2', 'Trigonometry & Data Interpretation', 6, 40, 'A company''s annual sales (in ₹ lakh) across five products are: A = 120, B = 80, C = 150, D = 100, E = 50. Find what percentage of the total sales product C contributes.', 'First find the total sales, then compute the required product''s share as a percentage of the total: `(value/total) × 100`.

Total `= 120 + 80 + 150 + 100 + 50 = 500`. Product C''s share `= 150/500 × 100 = 30%`.

The answer is **30%**.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');
